+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title>Start a Record — The Citizen's Record</title><meta name="description" content="Build a source-linked record of what is known, alleged, and still unknown."><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body>
+<header class="site-header"><div class="container nav-row"><a href="index.html" class="brand"><img src="logo.svg" alt=""><span class="brand-text">The Citizen's Record<small>Evidence Before Opinion</small></span></a><button class="nav-toggle" aria-label="Toggle menu" aria-expanded="false">☰</button><nav class="primary" aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="index.html">Start here</a><a href="the-record.html">The Record</a><a href="toolkit.html">Toolkit</a><a href="learn.html">Learn</a><a href="about.html">Standards</a><a href="contact.html">Contact</a><a href="record-builder.html" class="nav-cta">Start a record</a></nav></div></header>
+<main id="main-content"><section class="page-hero builder-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb">Record Builder / New record</div><h1>Build a record you can check.</h1><p>Begin with one question. Add the first source you find. Label what is known and what is not.</p></div></section>
+<section class="builder-section"><div class="container builder-layout"><div class="builder-intro"><span class="eyebrow">A guided workspace</span><h2>Start small. Stay honest.</h2><p>This lightweight record is for organizing research. It does not provide legal advice or decide what a document means for you.</p><div class="builder-steps"><div class="builder-step active"><span>01</span><div><strong>Question</strong><small>What are you trying to understand?</small></div></div><div class="builder-step"><span>02</span><div><strong>Source</strong><small>Where did the information originate?</small></div></div><div class="builder-step"><span>03</span><div><strong>Evidence</strong><small>What does the document actually show?</small></div></div><div class="builder-step"><span>04</span><div><strong>Unknown</strong><small>What remains unanswered?</small></div></div></div><div class="truth-card compact"><span class="eyebrow">Truth Standard</span><p>Use labels to keep a source, an allegation, an inference, and an unknown from collapsing into one statement.</p><div class="truth-badge-row"><span class="truth-badge fact">FACT</span><span class="truth-badge claim">CLAIM</span><span class="truth-badge unknown">UNKNOWN</span></div></div></div>
+<div class="builder-card"><div class="builder-card-head"><div><span class="docket">New record · saved locally</span><h3 id="builder-title">What are you trying to understand?</h3></div><span id="builder-progress" class="progress-label">01 / 04</span></div><form id="record-form"><label for="record-question">Your question</label><textarea id="record-question" name="question" placeholder="Example: What action did the agency formally take?" required></textarea><p class="field-help">Make it specific enough that a document could help answer it.</p><label for="record-source">First source (optional for now)</label><input id="record-source" name="source" type="url" placeholder="https://official-source.example/document"><p class="field-help">Prefer the original authority, order, docket, statute, meeting record, or dataset.</p><div class="builder-actions"><button type="submit" class="btn">Save and continue →</button></div><p id="builder-status" class="form-status" role="status"></p></form><div id="record-summary" class="record-summary" hidden><span class="eyebrow">Record started</span><h3 id="summary-question"></h3><div class="summary-grid"><div><span class="label">Source</span><p id="summary-source"></p></div><div><span class="label">Next step</span><p>Add one piece of evidence and label what remains unknown.</p></div></div><a href="index.html" class="text-link">Return to the method →</a></div></div></div></section>
+<section class="cta-band"><div class="container"><span class="docket on-dark">Keep going</span><h2>A record is stronger when it shows its limits.</h2><p>Come back to update the source, evidence, findings, and unknowns as your research develops.</p><a href="toolkit.html" class="btn ghost">Open the Toolkit →</a></div></section></main>
+<footer class="site-footer"><div class="container footer-bottom"><span>© 2026 The Citizen's Record. Educational use—not legal advice.</span><span><a href="about.html">Truth Standard</a> · <a href="contact.html">Send a correction</a></span></div></footer><script src="main.js"></script></body></html>
