-        <span class="eyebrow">Toolkit 03</span>
-        <h2>File a FOIA Request</h2>
-        <div class="steps">
-          <div class="step"><h4>Identify the right agency</h4><p>FOIA covers federal agencies only — states have their own public records laws.</p></div>
-          <div class="step"><h4>Write a specific request</h4><p>Vague requests get delayed. Name the records, date range, and format you want.</p></div>
-          <div class="step"><h4>Submit and log it</h4><p>Most agencies have an online portal. Save your confirmation and tracking number.</p></div>
-          <div class="step"><h4>Know your appeal rights</h4><p>A denial isn't final — administrative appeals have their own short deadlines.</p></div>
-        </div>
-      </div>
-      <div>
-        <span class="eyebrow">Toolkit 04</span>
-        <h2>Public Outreach to Representatives</h2>
-        <div class="steps">
-          <div class="step"><h4>Town halls</h4><p>Public meetings are recorded and often livestreamed — find the schedule.</p></div>
-          <div class="step"><h4>Public comment periods</h4><p>Agencies must accept and consider comments on proposed rules — this is your formal input.</p></div>
-          <div class="step"><h4>Written testimony</h4><p>Committees often accept written testimony from the public on pending bills.</p></div>
-          <div class="step"><h4>Coalition letters</h4><p>Organized, signed letters from constituent groups carry more institutional weight.</p></div>
-        </div>
