+<section><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Research tools</span><h2>Find the record behind the story.</h2></div></div><div class="grid cols-2"><a class="guide-card" href="record-builder.html?guide=find-government-documents"><span class="route-icon">01</span><span class="card-tag">Research tools</span><h3>Finding government documents</h3><p>Start with the institution that created the record instead of a summary about it.</p><span class="text-link">Open field manual →</span></a><a class="guide-card" href="record-builder.html?guide=read-a-docket"><span class="route-icon">02</span><span class="card-tag">Research tools</span><h3>How to read a docket</h3><p>Use a case number to trace filings, orders, judgments, and procedural history.</p><span class="text-link">Open field manual →</span></a></div></div></section>
+<section class="alt"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Public records</span><h2>Make the process traceable.</h2></div></div><div class="grid cols-2"><a class="guide-card" href="record-builder.html?guide=public-records-request"><span class="route-icon">03</span><span class="card-tag">Public records</span><h3>Making a public-records request</h3><p>Ask for defined records, narrow the time range, and log the response process.</p><span class="text-link">Open field manual →</span></a><a class="guide-card" href="record-builder.html?guide=follow-public-money"><span class="route-icon">04</span><span class="card-tag">Public records</span><h3>Following public money</h3><p>Use contracts, budgets, and campaign-finance systems to trace a claim back to a record.</p><span class="text-link">Open field manual →</span></a></div></div></section>
+<section><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Verification</span><h2>Know what the evidence can—and cannot—say.</h2></div></div><div class="grid cols-2"><a class="guide-card" href="record-builder.html?guide=verify-a-claim"><span class="route-icon">05</span><span class="card-tag">Verification</span><h3>How to verify a claim</h3><p>Separate a statement from the evidence offered for it, then work backward to the original record.</p><span class="text-link">Open field manual →</span></a><div class="truth-card"><span class="eyebrow">Truth Standard</span><h3>Label the record as you go.</h3><p>Use FACT, LAW, CLAIM, QUESTION, INFERENCE, and UNKNOWN to keep evidence separate from interpretation.</p><a class="text-link" href="record-builder.html">See it inside the Builder →</a></div></div></div></section>
